  "name": "Question 2",
  "problem": "Consider the function $f(x)=4{x}^{5}+5{x}^{4}-10{x}^{2}-20x+30.$ Given that ${f}^{\u2032}(-1)=0,$ which of the following statements are true?\n\n- ${f}^{\u2033}(-1)<0$\n- $f(x)$ has a relative minimum at $x=-1$\n- $f(x)$ has a relative maximum at $x=-1$",
  "worked_solution": "We're given that $x=-1$ is a stationary point of $f(x).$ We will use the second derivative test to classify this stationary point.\n\nCalculating the first derivative for the function $f(x)=4{x}^{5}+5{x}^{4}-10{x}^{2}-20x+30,$ we get\n\n$$\n{f}^{\u2032}(x)=20({x}^{4}+{x}^{3}-x-1).\n$$\n\nCalculating the second derivative, we get \n\n$$\n{f}^{\u2033}(x)=20(4{x}^{3}+3{x}^{2}-1).\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x=-1,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{\u2033}(-1) & =20(4(-1)^{3}+3(-1)^{2}-1) \\\\  & =20(-4+3-1) \\\\  & =-40<0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the second derivative is negative, we conclude that $f(x)$ has a relative maximum at $x=-1.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\"",
